      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T22:08:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can\u0027t reference arbitrary file paths from asflags, so I think you\u0027ll need the genrule.  If you want to have the .S file checked in you could make the genrule use `sed s\"MANIFEST_DATA\"$(in)\"` to rewrite the .S file with the path.\n\nThis always going to be hacky though, Soong doesn\u0027t know that compiling the .S file is going to read the `trusty_security_vm_signed` binary, and you\u0027re just hoping that the `static_libs: [\"trusty_security_vm_signed\"]` is going to cause the same file to be present at the same location when the `security_vm_signed_obj` rule is run in the RBE sandbox.",
      "parentUuid": "15e242c1_21a741db",
      "revId": "18a28b4401f0304b0b97ec1715a327b8af8d1ffc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
